    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d123-a1-a12">

                <pb facs="0402" n="344" xml:id="pg344"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">From the constitutional governor of the State of
                        Durango</hi>.</head>
                <p>As a satisfactory reply to your communication of yesterday, inquiring as to my
                    opinion of the <hi rendition="#italic">coup d état</hi> of Juarez, the manner in
                    which it impressed me, and my projected line of conduct for the future, I
                    herewith transmit to you a copy of a letter which I forwarded to Senor Juarez
                    from Presidio del Norte, dated December 15, of the past year.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left">Independence and liberty! <placeName>San
                            Antonio</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-02-04"
                            >February 4, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>J. M. PATONI.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The Citizen J. G. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ortega, <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constitutional President of the Republic of Mexico</hi></hi>,</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
